Z||000000||daved||07-08-2000||12:40 AM||||I tried to change the passenger side rack bushing tonight on my '86GT.  Got all the bits apart, only to discover, after I "modified" the rack casting to get at the circlip, (anyone got a smart way to do this?) that my bushing is hardened steel!<BR>Could this be an remanufactured rack? Or is there some gizzmo in front of the bushing?<BR>I hit it pretty hard with punch in one of the 3 grooves it has, and its very firmly mounted.<P>Sorry Rodney, but I dont think your aluminum bushing will fix this rack.  Time to visit the Boneyards again.  Dave||||reg||1
